Upstream Submodules, Datasets, and Attributions
=============================================================================

1. HackerTube Dataset (https://hackertube.org/data)
   Created by Andrej Karpathy, derived from open-index/hacker-news
   (https://huggingface.co/datasets/open-index/hacker-news).
   Licensed under Open Data Commons Attribution License (ODC-By 1.0):
   https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/by/1-0/
   Modified: Extracted canonical YouTube video IDs and channel names into
   extension/assets/seeds/hn-videos.txt and hn-channels.txt.

2. AiSList (vendor/AiSList - https://github.com/Override92/AiSList)
   Created by Override92 and contributors.
   Licensed under Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International
   (CC BY-NC 4.0): https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/
   Non-commercial use only. Provided as-is without warranties.
   Modified: Normalized channel handles and IDs into
   extension/assets/seeds/slop-channels.txt.

3. DeArrow Community Database (https://github.com/ajayyy/DeArrow)
   Created by Ajay Ramachandran and DeArrow contributors.
   Data licensed under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
   (CC BY-SA 4.0): https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
   Queried via k-anonymous 4-character SHA-256 hash prefixes against the public
   read-only mirror (https://dearrow.minibomba.pro/sbserver/).

4. Control Panel for Twitter (vendor/control-panel-for-twitter -
   https://github.com/insin/control-panel-for-twitter)
   Copyright (c) Jonathan Buchanan (insin). Licensed under the MIT License.

5. Slop Filter for X (vendor/slop-filter-for-x -
   https://github.com/midego1/slop-filter-for-x)
   Licensed under the MIT License.

6. FocusTube (vendor/FocusTube - https://github.com/malekwael229/FocusTube)
   Copyright (c) Malek Wael. Licensed under the MIT License.

7. xrai / rai (vendor/xrai - https://github.com/phuaky/xrai)
   Licensed under the MIT License.

8. JetBrains Mono (https://www.jetbrains.com/lp/mono/)
